      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 3 Stapleton Place, Dundalk, Co. Louth. A magnificent Georgian townhouse with self-contained basement residence. \r\n\r\nBlue Sky Property are delighted to present No. 3 Stapleton Place, a truly exceptional four-bedroom Georgian townhouse arranged over three storeys above a self-contained one-bedroom basement apartment. Meticulously renovated to an exacting standard by its current owners and interior designers, this impressive protected period residence blends elegant original character with contemporary luxury. From the grand stone approach and ornate wrought-iron railings to the refined interiors, high ceilings and carefully considered finishes, this is town-centre living at its most distinguished. Properties of this calibre, finish and location rarely come to the market. \r\n\r\nNo. 3 Stapleton Place offers an outstanding private home, a compelling multi-generational living opportunity, or a valuable investment with potential gross rental income in the region of €40,000 per annum. \r\n\r\nThe Main Residence -  A distinctive period portique frames the entrance, opening into an inviting front hallway where the original staircase rises through the upper floors. The home retains the proportions, detail and atmosphere expected of a fine Georgian residence, enhanced by a complete modern renovation. The centrepiece is the exceptional open-plan kitchen, dining and living room, measuring approximately 8.2m x 4.5m. This beautifully designed space enjoys a dual aspect, with views across Stapleton Place to the front and over the private gravel courtyard to the rear. The contemporary fitted kitchen is both stylish and practical, while a fully fitted utility room with direct courtyard access completes the ground-floor accommodation. \r\n\r\nThe first floor provides a generously proportioned principal bedroom to the front, complete with fitted wardrobes and a luxurious en-suite bathroom. A second bedroom overlooks the rear courtyard, with a family bathroom and hot press also located at this level. \r\nThe upper floor offers two additional double bedrooms, each providing versatile accommodation for family living, guests, home working or further rental potential. \r\n\r\nAccommodation : \r\nMain House:\r\nPorch: 1.92m x 1.92m\r\nHall: 1.85m x 7.37m\r\nLiving Room: 4.13m x 4.65m\r\nKitchen: 4.13m x 2.29m\r\nUtility Room: 2.18m x 2.70m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\nHall: 2.31m x 5.58m\r\nBathroom: 2.31m x 1.82m\r\nBedroom One: 4.12m x 3.05m\r\nBedroom Two: 4.62m x 3.80m\r\nEn-suite: 1.80m x 4.15m\r\n\r\nSecond Floor:\r\nHall: 1.8m x 4.52m\r\nBathroom: 1.80 x 3.91m\r\nBedroom Three: 4.12m x 3.32m\r\nBedroom Four: 4.13m x 3.53m \r\n\r\n\r\nNo. 3A Basement Flat - The self-contained one-bedroom basement flat has its own private front-door access and has also undergone a comprehensive renovation in recent years. The accommodation includes a spacious entrance hall, comfortable living room, double bedroom, galley kitchen and bathroom. A rear door opens directly to the shared gravel courtyard. Finished with the same strong eye for colour, comfort and design as the main residence, this is a particularly attractive element of the property for an investor, extended family, guest accommodation or supplementary income. \r\n\r\nThe apartment is currently rented and generates an annual rental income of €13,800. The existing tenancy will not be affected by the sale.\r\n\r\nAccommodation :\r\nPatio: 4.02m x 1.58m\r\nHall: 2m x 6.76m\r\nLiving Room: 3.93m x 4.19m\r\nBedroom: 3.92m x 3.05m\r\nKitchen: 2.18m x 4.69m\r\nHall: 0.95m x 2.75m\r\nBathroom: 1.14m x 2.65m\r\n\r\nOutdoor Space -  To the rear lies a private, south-facing gravel courtyard—an elegant and low-maintenance outdoor setting ideal for al fresco dining and entertaining. The front of the property is defined by its classic Georgian façade, grand stone steps, ornamental railings and distinctive entrance portique. Location Stapleton Place and the adjoining Roden Place form one of Dundalk’s most prestigious and historic Georgian terraces. This outstanding town-centre address places cafés, restaurants, bars, boutiques, schools, colleges, public transport and daily amenities within an easy stroll. \r\n\r\n Viewing strictly by appointment For all further details contact Blue Sky Property, Dundalk : 042 932 9333. Guide Price €500,000.\r\n\r\nBlue Sky Property and their servants or agents assume no responsibility for and give no guarantees, undertakings or warranties concerning the accuracy, completeness or up to date nature of the information and do not accept any liability whatsoever arising from any errors or omissions. The information does not constitute or form part of a contract and cannot be relied on as a representation of fact. Subject to contract / contract denied. Please note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate, and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
